WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:05.160
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
on Gotham we learned about one of the next

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.540
big Batman Villains the show is going to do,
as well as the beginning of all the current

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:10.590
comic book characters rise to power.

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:14.340
This was also the first episode they produced
since the pilot was ordered to series.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:18.141
So if you noticed any minor changes in the
way characters behaved or the look of the

00:00:18.141 --> 00:00:19.429
show that’s why.

00:00:19.429 --> 00:00:23.060
So just like normal I’ll start with top
5 moments, then explain any of the bigger

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:25.490
comic book references and then do my review.

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:27.199
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
the episode.

00:00:27.199 --> 00:00:30.390
I’ll wait just a sec...okay, here we go.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:33.450
Number 5 - Professor Pyg Shoutout

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:36.090
In Fish Mooney’s Club, the bartender’s
name is Lazlo.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:39.170
Lazlo Valentin in the comics is Professor
Pyg.

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:44.050
They might be doing something different with
the character because Professor Pyg is associated

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:46.270
with the Circus of Strange.

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:53.620
I guess this is a prequel show, so you could
say that he just hasn’t taken on that persona

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:54.620
yet.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.100
Pyg is a noted brilliant chemist.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:59.730
So it makes sense they’d tease him in a
story involving a date rape drug.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:04.690
Grant Morrison created him in this story that
involved Pyg creating this mindless army of

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:09.020
lobotomized genderless doll-people called
Dollotrons.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:16.240
I know there was a Dollmaker reference so
it was a little confusing.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.080
But the Pyg storyline also involved a drug
so there’s a lot of mixed references you

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:21.080
could drawn.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.979
Add to that they pig mask we saw.

00:01:23.979 --> 00:01:26.271
Number 4 - Bruce Wayne is Testing Himself

00:01:26.271 --> 00:01:33.929
There’s a lot you could say about the Bruce
Wayne storyline in the series.

00:01:33.929 --> 00:01:37.149
Because we know exactly where this character
is headed it’s a little strange watching

00:01:37.149 --> 00:01:39.479
it play out in episodes.

00:01:39.479 --> 00:01:42.770
Because of that I just kind of separate myself
from the comics and the movies when I’m

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:48.780
watching David Mazouz the actor.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:57.110
In the context of the episode, I totally bought
that he’d be doing disturbing drawings in

00:01:57.110 --> 00:01:58.289
his notepad and listening to crazy hardcore
music.

00:01:58.289 --> 00:02:00.960
It’s just his way of processing the trauma.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:04.719
If you thought his acting was a little weird
when he was talking to Gordon, think about

00:02:04.719 --> 00:02:05.859
it this way.

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:09.840
Bruce Wayne is the mask the Batman wears when
he’s in public.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:16.250
So Bruce Wayne the child, is in the process
of creating the fake Bruce Wayne he let’s

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:17.520
the world see.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:21.470
So I think him being a little wooden in scenes
is the actor consciously making the character

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:23.720
look like he’s acting to gordon.

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:28.930
It would be like you putting on a facade to
talk to someone versus just being yourself.

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:33.330
I don’t think Batman really knows who he
is and I don’t think he wants to know.

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:34.900
So just keep that in mind.

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:38.920
It’s David Mazouz playing a character who’s
playing a character.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:50.769
Bruce Wayne is playing Fake Bruce Wayne.

00:02:50.769 --> 00:02:55.590
Number 3 - The Penguin Begins Kidnapping and
Extorting People for Money

00:02:55.590 --> 00:03:00.290
We are now seeing the beginnings of what will
become the Penguin’s penchant for extortion.

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:02.450
He evolves into something of a white collar
criminal.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:08.900
Or at least he’ll exclusively target the
wealthy but we’re seeing him figure it out.

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:13.930
I’m still wrapping my brain around Robin
Lord Taylor’s character.

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:15.379
He seems like he’s pretty vicious.

00:03:15.379 --> 00:03:16.909
I believed he was going to carve that dude’s
eyes out.

00:03:16.909 --> 00:03:22.540
He murdered the fisherman, so it stands to
reason he’d also cut up his kidnapping victim.

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:28.630
The interesting thing is the debt he still
owes to Gordon for sparing his life and how

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:32.780
that will tie in with all the “external
villain forces” that Falcone teased in the

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:33.780
first episode.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:41.010
Those are our batman villains we have yet
to meet.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:43.330
Including the Dollmaker.

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:47.450
At some point, penguin will have to cross
paths with Gordon again, whether he comes

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:51.680
back to gotham first or Gordon finds him on
the outskirts of town.

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:56.849
I think the Penguin will end up repaying his
debt this season by helping Gordon take down

00:03:56.849 --> 00:03:58.769
some of these bigger batman villains.

00:03:58.769 --> 00:04:03.960
I don’t see anything big happening to Falcone,
because in the timeline, he’s still around

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:13.440
when Bruce Wayne is in college, which is like
8 years away.

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:16.590
Number 2 - Catwoman emeds herself with Team
Batman

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:20.780
I’m really digging Camren Bicondova so far
as Selina Kyle.

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:29.870
Her task is to play the street urchin who’s
smarter than most of the adults on the show.

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:33.962
As evidenced by the way she worked that police
officer who brought in Gordon at the end of

00:04:33.962 --> 00:04:34.962
the episode.

00:04:34.962 --> 00:04:36.139
She’s in the process of embedding herself
as an ally to Team Batman.

00:04:36.139 --> 00:04:43.199
She called Bruce “The Boy”, so I’m excited
to see what kind of trouble they cause together

00:04:43.199 --> 00:04:44.199
eventually.

00:04:44.199 --> 00:04:47.699
I wonder if the Bruce Testing himself arc
will throw him into her path.

00:04:47.699 --> 00:04:50.190
Like he’ll try something crazy, and she’ll
be there to bail him out.

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:51.190
And they’ll start being friends.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:52.190
It’s still too soon to tell, but Catwoman
plays both sides of the fence in the comics,

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:53.190
so she could inform on Gordon for Falcone
or one of the other villains if she thought

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:54.190
she had to.

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:55.990
and my Number 1 moment - Dollmaker Shoutout

00:04:55.990 --> 00:04:59.800
The two guest stars Doug and Patti were working
for the Dollmaker.

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:04.060
They were rounding up children for him, it
might turn into a doll army situation.

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:06.820
Like they’d do the professor pyg storyline
where they turn everyone into mindless slaves.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:09.349
Otherwise why would they need all those children?

00:05:09.349 --> 00:05:13.389
We’ll see more of Dollmaker in the future,
he’s just one of many Batman villains coming

00:05:13.389 --> 00:05:14.389
to the show.

00:05:14.389 --> 00:05:19.020
It sounds like he’ll be one of the big ‘external
forces’ Falcone was talking about.

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:20.979
Another big one is Hugo Strange.

00:05:20.979 --> 00:05:26.370
He’s tied more to the Arkham storyline,
and that only got teased.

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:31.240
So I’ll talk more Arkham when it shows up
in an episode.

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:34.509
But it will, they’re doing Arkham this year.

00:05:34.509 --> 00:05:36.169
Let me know what your favorite moment was.

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:40.160
And how do you think that Selina Kyle and
Bruce will meet for the first time.

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:45.840
It will be like a Batman meet cute where they
both trip over the criminals they’re beating

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:46.840
up and bonk heads like in a romantic comedy.

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:49.082
“Oh, I’m sorry, I was just beating information
out of this guy...I was doing the same thing…”

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:50.139
Here’s a few Comic Book References I spotted:

00:05:50.139 --> 00:05:54.690
I already mentioned Arkham, Professor Pyg
and The Dollmaker, but the group of kids Bruce

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:59.290
wanted to help are probably going to be the
precursor to the Child Care Facility he creates,

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:03.680
I think he has a boy’s home he funds in
the movies.

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:06.129
But I’d imagine he also funds one for girls
too.

00:06:06.129 --> 00:06:09.930
It’s just the beginning of him using his
money to help people.

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:13.830
You don’t always see it in the comics, but
Bruce Wayne is like Bill Gates when it comes

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:16.090
to giving his money away to charitable causes.

00:06:16.090 --> 00:06:19.970
He even funds the Outsiders Super Hero Group.

00:06:19.970 --> 00:06:20.970
Carol Kane as The Penguin’s Mother is amazing.

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:21.970
Kabelput is what she said.

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:24.410
I’m assuming The Penguin changed it to sound
more American.

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:43.770
There was aslo some more of The Riddler who
got wrapped up in the Arkham reference 

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:45.730
and the ATP drug.

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:52.220
It’s also possible Hugo Strange could be
tied to that drug plot too.

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:58.169
I don’t know which episode he’s going
to debut in.

00:06:58.169 --> 00:07:03.389
There were several Joker references with people
yelling Clown, even Oswald on the phone at

00:07:03.389 --> 00:07:04.389
the end.

00:07:04.389 --> 00:07:11.509
I felt like this trident was a reference to
either Trident the villain or Aquaman’s

00:07:11.509 --> 00:07:12.509
Trident.

00:07:12.509 --> 00:07:15.389
He’s not coming on the show, it’s just
that there are only a few Trident’s in the

00:07:15.389 --> 00:07:16.960
DC Universe.

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:21.180
Someone told me on twitter they saw a Queen
Industries Logo, I didn’t catch it but I

00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:22.180
believe it.

